  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Showers and thunderstorms this afternoon through Saturday,\n   focused I-90 southward. Gusty outflow winds today, locally\n   heavy rain concern on Friday.\n\n-  Warming and drying Sunday through early next week.\n\n\nThis Afternoon through Saturday: An upper-level low spinning over\nNorthern California will draw deep moisture into the region \nthrough this evening, driving precipitable water (PWAT) values to \n150-200% of normal. Morning cloud cover has kept instability\ntempered thus far but partial clearing is still expected to allow\nfor multiple rounds of showers and thunderstorms focused I-90 \nsouthward. Across Lemhi and southern Idaho counties, 30-40 kt of \ndeep- layer shear will support a few strong thunderstorms capable \nof producing hail and damaging winds. Outside of these strong \ncells, general storms will frequently produce 25-35 mph outflow \ngusts and brief heavy rain.\n\nElevated instability and broad synoptic lift will sustain showers\nand isolated thunderstorms Friday morning, concentrated south of \nI-90. Additional convective rounds will redevelop Friday afternoon\nand evening. Heavy rainfall will be the primary threat on Friday,\nwith localized rates exceeding 0.75 in/hr. This poses a threat \nfor localized runoff and debris flows over burn scars and other \nvulnerable terrain. One complicating factor could be cloud cover\nmuting instability but broad scale lift will lead to considerable\nshowers and at least some thunderstorm activity. \n\nThe upper low will slide through southern Idaho Friday night into\nSaturday, delivering a period of wrap-around stratiform rain \nalong the I-90 corridor southward to Lemhi County, before \nprecipitation tapers off late Saturday.\n\nSunday through Mid-Next Week: Ensemble guidance shows high \nconfidence (90-100%) in upper-level ridging building across the \nregion Sunday and Monday, bringing a notable warming and drying \ntrend. Although detail guidance diverges Tuesday through late next\nweek, the broad ensemble pattern favors southwesterly flow, mild \ntemperatures, and a gradual reintroduction of thunderstorm \nchances.",
